      "type": "feat",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>The mosslax leaps into the air and lands in a space within 20 feet of it, attempting to crush anything beneath it. <em>Saving Throw:</em> DC 20 Dexterity, each creature in the mosslax's destination space. <em>Failure:</em> 39 (6d12) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is knocked Prone, is Restrained, and unable to breathe until it no longer shares a space with the mosslax. <em>Success:</em> The target escapes and moves to the nearest unoccupied space within 5 feet of the mosslax.</p><p>A creature can take an action to make a DC 20 Strength (Athletics) check, freeing itself or another creature trapped under the mosslax within its reach on a success.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
